    <string name="sync_help_guide_title">MoYue Cloud &amp; WebDAV Guide</string>
    <string name="sync_help_section1_title">1. Roles of Two Cloud Targets</string>
    <string name="sync_help_section1_body">1. MoYue Cloud (Default): Used for real-time syncing of reading progress, bookmarks, and highlights across devices.\n2. WebDAV Cloud: Ideal as a large ebook repository, supporting Baidu Netdisk, Quark, Aliyun Drive, Nutstore, Synology NAS, etc.</string>
    <string name="sync_help_section2_title">2. What is AList? How to connect?</string>
    <string name="sync_help_section2_body">AList is a powerful open-source file list program supporting multiple storage providers (alist.nn.ci).\n\nIt mounts your Baidu Netdisk, Aliyun Drive, Quark, etc. and provides a standard WebDAV endpoint.\n\n• Format: enter \"http://server_ip:port/dav\" (with /dav) with your credentials.\n• Documentation: https://alist.nn.ci</string>
    <string name="sync_help_section3_title">3. Bookmarks &amp; Highlights Guarantee</string>
    <string name="sync_help_section3_body">When uploading books to WebDAV, MoYue uploads the EPUB and automatically creates a companion metadata file (.moreader.json).\n\nWhen downloading from WebDAV on any device, reading progress, bookmarks, and highlights are fully restored!</string>
